{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants","id":900642,"title":"[2E] Option - High Speech Variants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-26T20:50:38-07:00","id":900642,"title":"[2E] Option - High Speech Variants","content":"I generally like changes of 2E <b>Mage</b> at all. However, I very much was downed that High Speech Forms were taken out of game - and I could not made character that shout 'Expelliarmus!', only some weird sounds of 'Glossolalia'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This should look like that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/harrypotter/images/b/b0/Harry_disarms_Lucius.gif/revision/latest?cb=20160114190837\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> It's odd, when all rest of <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> 'spell factors' material clearly become Yantras mechanics. So this topic is to recreate those in 2E rules and pointing to logical implications of those on setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of Mysteries, p.92</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Accented: </b>The Accented form is superimposed on normal speech. The mage speaks a chosen language with particular in\ufb02ections so that it acts as an occult \u201ccarrier wave\u201d for the hidden \u201ccode\u201d of High Speech. Mages using this form appear to be speaking normal words in a strange accent. The cadence, tone and associated body language convey the magical import of the language. This makes it seem strangely accented (and often archaic) to Sleepers. Sleepers can repeat these speech patterns to repeat the \u201csecret codes,\u201d and other mages and beings who look for High Speech (such as ancient Artifacts, spirits and tomb guardians) will understand.<br /> <br /> The speech in the carrier language does not have the same meaning as that conveyed through High Speech accent, but Awakened witnesses can easily discern the secrets so conveyed. Mages who come from cultures that especially honor a living language prefer this form. It is sometimes called the Awakened version of a language (\u201cAwakened Japanese,\u201d for instance). Users often believe that it is the true form of High Speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of Mysteries, p.92</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Poetic:</b> Neither a matter of pronunciation or accent, Poetic High Speech is a matter of imagery and enigmas. The Poetic form is a vocabulary of images and symbols that can be expressed in any language, along with a meter that binds it into memorable performance. These signs and phrases evoke the necessary meanings in a mage\u2019s mind, but not a Sleeper\u2019s. Only mages have the necessary backgrounds to recognize a metaphor for the High Speech word for a magical operation. Furthermore, similar to Accented High Speech, Poetic High Speech recalls distinct rhythms and tones, binding the Poetic form into a cohesive form of magic and communication. Cultures with a powerful oral tradition tend to produce mages who use this form. They are more than willing to embrace the rhythmic conventions and the thousands of symbols that they must use.<br /> <br /> Even if an Awakened sorcerer is exposed to a form for the \ufb01rst time, she gains instant pro\ufb01ciency in it within seconds of exposure, as if she suddenly remembers a long life lived in a land where the form was the native tongue. Otherwise, regardless of form, all spoken High Speech conforms to the rules in <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And basic rule from Tome of Mysteries for those:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of Mysteries, p.91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of culture or preference, every mage can use and understand every form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking in account that in 2E Peripheral Mage Sight is translating all the time High Speech as collection of Symbols in speech for Awakened, I'm still confused why we need to lost Accented and Poetic forms in first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-29-2016, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T04:55:47-07:00","id":900832,"title":"","content":"There's literally nothing saying it's been taken out and you are overreacting as usual. The original 1e book didn't mention them either.<br /> <br /> In fact, Dark Eras mentions them in passing on pg.79.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:16:53-07:00","id":900838,"title":"","content":"if you want to yell spell names at people, it's a perfectly viable Shadow Name yantra. &quot;My spells have names, and I shout them while casting&quot; is a good persona tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:29:23-07:00","id":900848,"title":"","content":"A good reason why High Speech doesn't have different forms now is because its actually a language. IIRC, Supernal critters are fluent speakers of it, and London is covered in runes that anyone with Mage Sight can read.<br /> <br /> And, to be fair, chanting in High Speech takes longer than a single shout like that - we're dealing with something beyond the realm of bastardized latin being called out with an attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-27-2016, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T05:45:18-07:00","id":900856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=900848#post900848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good reason why High Speech doesn't have different forms now is because its actually a language. IIRC, Supernal critters are fluent speakers of it, and London is covered in runes that anyone with Mage Sight can read.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly not a language, it's glossolalia. Also, runes were a thing in 1e. That's what all those symbols covering the line are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:45:09-07:00","id":900901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=900856#post900856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's explicitly not a language, it's glossolalia.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds as glossolalia to sleepers, but with mages &quot;it is useable in spoken and written form as a crude form of communication&quot;. Page 90.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:10:10-07:00","id":900922,"title":"","content":"In 1e, it wasn't explicitly a language. In 2e, we have beings that can and do use it as a language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:21:04-07:00","id":901391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=900901#post900901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds as glossolalia to sleepers, but with mages &quot;it is useable in spoken and written form as a crude form of communication&quot;. Page 90.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it can convey meaning, but it doesn't do so in the way a normal language does. The next setence: &quot;Because it\u2019s more the symbol of a language than a real language...&quot;. It's still sounds the same, it just makes sense on some intuitive level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 2e, we have beings that can and do use it as a language. </div> </div> </div>That was in 1e too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:28:38-07:00","id":901458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants#post900642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally like changes of 2E <b>Mage</b> at all. However, I very much was downed that High Speech Forms were taken out of game - and I could not made character that shout 'Expelliarmus!', only some weird sounds of 'Glossolalia'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... Shouting &quot;Expelliarmus&quot; is totally glossolalia. It's a made-up bunch of vowels and consonants that sounds kind of like a latinish word but doesn't actually have any linguistic meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants#post900642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's odd, when all rest of <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> 'spell factors' material clearly become Yantras mechanics. So this topic is to recreate those in 2E rules and pointing to logical implications of those on setting.<br /> <br /> And this...<br /> <br /> And basic rule from Tome of Mysteries for those:</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a cool Merit to me. Or even just describe your character's use of High Speech as a Yantra as sounding like a specific language, but with different inflections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants#post900642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking in account that in 2E Peripheral Mage Sight is translating all the time High Speech as collection of Symbols in speech for Awakened, I'm still confused why we need to lost Accented and Poetic forms in first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know as we did lose it. Verbal high speech can pretty much sound like anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T22:07:58-07:00","id":902491,"title":"","content":"I was confused on whole Glosolalia stuff, as I remembered from various horrors and fantasy movies as working like this...<br /> <br /> ( Look from 0:20 for a half minute )<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GAo0r4At42g\" data-code=\"GAo0r4At42g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GAo0r4At42g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But with Accented and Poetic usage of 1E High Speech they work much more like classical languages of their origin spelling. Asian sorcerer using <i>Awakened Japanese</i> is really incanting in Japanese. Well, 'almost Japaneses', in same way as wizards in Harry Potter use 'almost Latin'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:29:13-07:00","id":902510,"title":"","content":"You know in Stephen King's Insomnia, He had a pretty good idea of how it could work. Long story short. The characters have a talk with &quot;higher&quot; beings of Order and Chaos. but they didn't use 'words' or pharses or sentences. They used pictures emotions and idea. I'd imagen that High Speech is just like that. The words/characters mean nothing, its the symbolism behind them.<br /> <br /> High Speech is just a tool to shape the symbolism into what you want. Its why Technobabble works. The science is mostly theoretical and impossible to obverse, but the intention behind it shapes what you want.<br /> <br /> OHOH Wild idea, Phonic Alphabets are a tool of the lie. Back before Alphabets became widely used most people used pictures/pictograph to convey meanings and ideas. Sure we have more ideas, but now everything is more and more obscured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:46:59-07:00","id":902515,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, I think you're getting really hung up on the word glossolalia and missing the forest for the trees. Forget that word for a second. High Speech is the Supernal symbol of language. The speaker makes some noises and the listener understands the speaker's meaning, the specifics of those noises don't actually matter. If you want your High Speech to sound like weird Latin or weird Japanese, or whatever else, that's fine. Because the specific sounds the speaker makes don't actually matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-29-2016, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T00:32:37-07:00","id":902538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=902515#post902515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd, I think you're getting really hung up on the word glossolalia and missing the forest for the trees. Forget that word for a second. High Speech is the Supernal symbol of language. The speaker makes some noises and the listener understands the speaker's meaning, the specifics of those noises don't actually matter. If you want your High Speech to sound like weird Latin or weird Japanese, or whatever else, that's fine. Because the specific sounds the speaker makes don't actually matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not sure if this was RAI read of corebook. But it <i>does</i> have sense when Peripheral Mage Sight let you autotranslate it and higher levels of Mage Sight let observe Symbols. So I understand that High Speech is 'languages' of Symbols itself, and what exactly you say does not have any meaning?<br /> <br /> Then saying things in Sleepers languages with weird pronunciation could work then - as saying things as poetry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:40:50-07:00","id":902671,"title":"","content":"Sure, Mages would still auto-translate it and Sleepers would still remember it as gibbering though since High Speech is covered by Dissonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:15:29-07:00","id":902727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=902538#post902538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not sure if this was RAI read of corebook. But it <i>does</i> have sense when Peripheral Mage Sight let you autotranslate it and higher levels of Mage Sight let observe Symbols. So I understand that High Speech is 'languages' of Symbols itself, and what exactly you say does not have any meaning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Close. I'd say a more useful way to think about it is that what you say has meaning, but that meaning isn't attached to the words. The platonic ideal behind language is simply that the speaker speaks, and the listener understands. The words themselves are immaterial. So you communicate symbolic meaning with the things you say, which can be gibberish, or faux-Latin, or what ever else you want. The effect is the same regardless: the words themselves have no meaning to the listener - it might sound like made-up words, or like a language they're not familiar with. But, the sounds still evoke the intended symbolic meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=902538#post902538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then saying things in Sleepers languages with weird pronunciation could work then - as saying things as poetry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would certainly allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:17:45-07:00","id":902730,"title":"","content":"Have you ever listened to music written in a language you don't know, but still felt like you could kind of understand the emotions the artist was trying to express? That's kind of how I understand High Speech working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:42:38-07:00","id":902743,"title":"","content":"Some music composers make made-up pseudo-languages to put in their music exactly because of this effect. There is also an interesting psychological theory, that for everyone, their &quot;non-native language&quot; seems more expressive than the language they talk and conveys more emotion and feeling; this is attributed to the fact that due to you being unable to process the &quot;text&quot; of the speech, your perception focuses on more universal aspects of talking, which are supposed to surpass languages. Thus, for a person not speaking Japanese, listening to japanese anime with original audio and [their language] subtitles will feel more &quot;expressive&quot;, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://canta-per-me.net/lyrics/about-kajiurago/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://canta-per-me.net/lyrics/about-kajiurago/\" target=\"_blank\"> canta-per-me.net - A Yuki Kajiura Fansite &raquo; Lyrics &amp; Song Info &raquo; About Kajiurago </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://canta-per-me.net/lyrics/about-kajiurago/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://canta-per-me.net/lyrics/about-kajiurago/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-29-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:24:06-07:00","id":902971,"title":"","content":"So, in the end, whole topics idea is more like optional rule in corebook ruleset than proper hack? Or even it's the way how it <i>should</i> be played?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:35:12-07:00","id":902979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=902971#post902971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the end, whole topics idea is more like optional rule in corebook ruleset than proper hack? Or even it's the way how it <i>should</i> be played?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:37:35-07:00","id":902982,"title":"","content":"I will then have small request on PM to you then, <b>Char</b>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T21:29:43-07:00","id":963529,"title":"","content":"Small compilation of inspirations for those rules option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=29fvdnzZ0cw\" data-code=\"29fvdnzZ0cw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/29fvdnzZ0cw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T22:59:45-07:00","id":963561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=901458#post901458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Shouting &quot;Expelliarmus&quot; is totally glossolalia. It's a made-up bunch of vowels and consonants that sounds kind of like a latinish word but doesn't actually have any linguistic meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's meant to be &quot;Expelleo armam! (I drive off the weapon)&quot; but the conjugation and declension weren't done properly. To quote the other Harry, &quot;Damn Latin correspondence course&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T07:32:50-07:00","id":963687,"title":"","content":"Sorry to kinda hijack the thread, but I have an on-topic question so I'll just go ahead: <br /> <br /> I always assumed that High Speech was a language that, unlike others, had an intrinsic relationship between the symbol (words) and the meaning. So, in English the word is &quot;tree&quot;, but it could have been anything else, while in HS <b>tree</b> is <b>tree</b> because it couldn't be anything else. But reading this topic looks like I'm way off mark?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T00:07:36-07:00","id":964127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ehkesoyo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=963687#post963687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed that High Speech was a language that, unlike others, had an intrinsic relationship between the symbol (words) and the meaning. So, in English the word is &quot;tree&quot;, but it could have been anything else, while in HS <b>tree</b> is <b>tree</b> because it couldn't be anything else. But reading this topic looks like I'm way off mark?</div> </div> </div> </div>Second edition is a bit different in the flavour text.<br /> <br /> As a mage I think of the supernal symbol of trees, getting that pure meaning into my head and then I just make a sound. Perhaps &quot;Tagrus&quot; for the sake of having an example. Another mage hearing me has their magical senses flash and although they hear the sound &quot;Tagrus&quot; inside their head the supernal concept of trees just pops into their head magically. Doesn't matter if they speak a completely different language than me, they know what I meant. They're also not going to get confused like you can with a normal language, even if they're a mathematician they're not going to think that I mean logic trees because that's not the symbol I invoked even though in English the word &quot;Tree&quot; could refer to both meanings.<br /> <br /> There's no guarantee that tomorrow when I say the word tree again in High Speech that it'll be &quot;Tagrus&quot; again. Maybe tomorrow the word &quot;Saffam&quot; pops into my head instead when I think of the supernal symbol. If you try to say tree in High Speech maybe &quot;Volvandrigast&quot; seems right to you instead. It doesn't matter though because the word is conveyed directly and magically. It's why Sleepers can never understand High Speech, they can't memorize the words because there are no words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:05:49-07:00","id":964174,"title":"","content":"That's interesting. So HS isn't a language, it's just an ephemeral codification of a supernal concept. Can there be HS poetry, then? Innuendos? Word play? Metaphors?<br /> On the other hand, could a Mage with enough skill or power force that symbolism into a mundane code? Such as a painting of a landscape or any common language?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:16:56-07:00","id":964180,"title":"","content":"No poetry, innuendo, word play or metaphors. Has is only capable of communicating direct, simple messages and is impossible to lie in. In many ways despite being the idealization of language it's also less useful for actual communication than the languages that derive from it.<br /> <br /> As for messing with it via magic, that's pretty much the realm of Prime, Words of Truth for instance could easily be described as decoding HS so anyone can understand while manipulating it to convey more nuance as long as the message is true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-06-2016, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:29:33-07:00","id":964188,"title":"","content":"Huh... 1 Reach to make Words of True work in a non verbal code such as painting or music? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:32:15-07:00","id":964190,"title":"","content":"It works also with 'Accented High Speech' version from 1E <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> ( page 92 ), as character uses all the time the same original language for High Speech words.<br /> <br /> <b>Accented: </b><i>The Accented form is superimposed on normal speech. The mage speaks a chosen language with particular in\ufb02ections so that it acts as an occult \u201ccarrier wave\u201d for the hidden \u201ccode\u201d of High Speech. Mages using this form appear to be speaking normal words in a strange accent. The cadence, tone and associated body language convey the magical import of the language. This makes it seem strangely accented (and often archaic) to Sleepers. Sleepers can repeat these speech patterns to repeat the \u201csecret codes,\u201d and other mages and beings who look for High Speech (such as ancient Artifacts, spirits and tomb guardians) will understand.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The speech in the carrier language does not have the same meaning as that conveyed through High Speech accent, but Awakened witnesses can easily discern the secrets so conveyed. Mages who come from cultures that especially honor a living language prefer this form. It is sometimes called the Awakened version of a language (\u201cAwakened Japanese,\u201d for instance). Users often believe that it is the true form of High Speech.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:51:14-07:00","id":964198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ehkesoyo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=964188#post964188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... 1 Reach to make Words of True work in a non verbal code such as painting or music? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I don't think that works as of 2e, High Speech can't be repeated or heard by Sleepers seems pretty cut and dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T04:21:11-07:00","id":964211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=964198#post964198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I don't think that works as of 2e, High Speech can't be repeated or heard by Sleepers seems pretty cut and dry.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Accented High Speech you are <i>not</i> saying words in actual, let's say, Japanese. Awakened Japanese just sounds <i>a like</i> normal Japanese, but they are <i>not</i> the same.<br /> <br /> It's like with Latin and Harry Potter 'wizards Latin' - in HP series spells sounds a like Latin, but they truly are not. Even if on first hearing, made by the uneducated listener, they <i>can</i> sound as Latin to them. But Roman professor will clearly say to you they are just made up words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-06-2016, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T04:47:41-07:00","id":964217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants?p=964198#post964198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that works as of 2e, High Speech can't be repeated or heard by Sleepers seems pretty cut and dry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classical High Speech can't be. The point of accented high speech is that it's a variation with special properties. Note that High speech in the 1e core book was descibed in pretty much the same terms as it is in 2e with no hint that there were variations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:24:57-07:00","id":982041,"title":"","content":"When you are doing bad inflections on Latin and get High Speech instead... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/aN796TA.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:32:26-07:00","id":982170,"title":"","content":"Based on my reading of this it sounds like High Speech is the grammatical equivalent of an emoji language, except a High Speech word is not just a direct pictorial representation of the concept, like an emoji, but any direct expression that conveys it. Neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}